{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T12:33:53.859Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 1 implemented and verified.\n\n**Verify:** `node --import tsx --test tests/logger-status.test.ts` → 12 pass / 0 fail.\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/core/logger.ts`: `LoggerOptions.stream` gains `columns?: number`; added `fitStatusText()` that clamps to `(stream.columns ?? 80) - 2` with a `…`; `redraw()` now emits `CLEAR_LINE + frame + ' ' + fitted`; `status()` stores raw text so `[prefix]` never touches the status row.\n- `src/watcher/runner.ts`: `formatTaskStatusRow(taskNumber, stats)` no longer takes `terminalWidth` or truncates — it assembles the full row; removed the now-unused `STATUS_SPINNER_PREFIX_WIDTH`.\n- `tests/logger-status.test.ts`: `FakeStream` supports `columns`; status assertions expect un-prefixed text; added a columns-40/100-char exact-bytes test and a no-wrap/no-ghost redraw test.\n\n**Notes**\n- `formatIdleStatus` (in `src/watcher/loop.ts`, outside scope) already had no width param and no truncation, so that acceptance line holds without touching loop.ts.\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit` now has exactly one error at `tests/runner-terminal-status.test.ts:200` (passes a width arg to the 2-param function). That file is outside my scope and belongs to tasks 3/4; documented in the results file.\n\nResults written to `specs/015-status-row-fixes/.run/results/1.md`."}}
